    "innovation": "This study quantifies and maps historical and projected maximum temperature trends across *Pinus brutia* breeding zones in Turkey, revealing significant spatial warming variability to inform the development of climate-resilient, zone-specific tree breeding and genetic resource management strategies.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "SRTM",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "digital elevation data",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The study area was delineated based on the BZs of P. brutia to define elevation-based sub-zones within these major BZs, digital elevation data from the Shuttle Radar Topography Mission (SRTM, earthdata.nasa.gov/data/instruments/srtm) with a 30-meter spatial resolution were employed (Farr et al., 2007).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "TerraClimate",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Tmax",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "To assess historical trends in monthly average Tmax from 1960 to 2014 across the main BZs and their sub-zones, the TerraClimate (climatologylab. org/terraclimate.html) dataset (Monthly Climate and Climatic Water Balance for Global Terrestrial Surfaces developed by the University of Idaho) was employed (Abatzoglou et al., 2018).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "NEX-GDDP-CMIP6",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Tmax",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "For future climate projections spanning 2014 to 2100, the NASA Earth Exchange Global Daily Downscaled Climate Projections (NEX-GDDP-CMIP6) dataset was utilized (Thrasher et al., 2012). Daily Tmax values were aggregated to compute monthly averages, and units were converted from Kelvin to degrees Celsius to ensure consistency with historical records. Trends in projected monthly average Tmax were quantified for each pixel within the study area under the high-emission SSP5-8.5 scenario.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "UKESM1-0-LL",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Tmax",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Seven global climate models from the NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 ensemble were selected for analysis: UKESM1-0-LL, EC-Earth3, CanESM5, ACCESS-CM2, GFDL-ESM4, KIOST-ESM, and FGOALS. In order to understand variation in Tmax trends, average of the Tmax values was quantified within each sub-zone.",
